{
 "title": "Rear-port rebuild",
 "lede": "Back-top cut to the port corner, without its mounting brackets: the 9 mm ceiling, the rear wall and the east side wall, with the label tiles outside in channels between side rails. Inside are the four bulkheads, the ASSE chain out to a JG union tee on a 9.5 mm stub, the Pisco with a neoFit ACVUS-44 check in its outlet, the flow meter straight into the soda union, the meter's inlet turned straight down through production's R14 holder under 1 in foam, and the G Ganen carbonator pump where production stands it, without its elbows. V-K (amber), its stem elbow and its printed wall stand as production stands them, moved with the union tee; the wall reaches the side wall instead of the cap. The CO2 tube, red, leaves the check forward in one bend and comes straight down onto the cap between V-K and the pump. A shows the water split and V-K alone, G the CO2 tube among its neighbours, and H the tube over the carbonator, its coil and the two reservoirs under the cap. B and F are cut at X77.5, D at X60.",
